WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.757
Spark SQL still uses SQL-style NULL semantics.

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:08.952
Distributed execution does not make NULL easier or less important.

00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:13.522
Missing values affect comparisons, filters, joins, and aggregates.

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:17.937
The data-quality habits from Module 9 still apply in Spark.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:25.257
Many relational ideas transfer directly to Spark SQL: NULL semantics, date arithmetic, CTEs, joins, grouping,

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:26.087
and windows.

00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:32.907
Syntax details may differ, but the same reasoning about grain, missingness, and cardinality still applies.

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:39.520
Portability is easiest when the business rule is clear before dialect-specific tuning.
